From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:24:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clutter/text: Focus the input method out when disposing a
 focused text

ClutterText focuses the input method out from its key-focus-out handler,
but an actor that is destroyed while it has key focus never gets
key-focus-out. The input method then kept pointing at the destroyed
text, and the next surrounding text request, such as the one after
switching input sources, read freed memory.

Focus the input method out when a text that still has it focused is
disposed.
---
 clutter/clutter/pango/clutter-text.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/clutter/clutter/pango/clutter-text.c b/clutter/clutter/pango/clutter-text.c
index c7566e30f..efdd9aeba 100644
--- a/clutter/clutter/pango/clutter-text.c
+++ b/clutter/clutter/pango/clutter-text.c
@@ -1952,6 +1952,9 @@ clutter_text_dispose (GObject *gobject)
 
   g_clear_handle_id (&priv->password_hint_id, mtk_source_remove);
 
+  if (clutter_input_focus_is_focused (priv->input_focus))
+    clutter_input_method_focus_out (clutter_backend_get_input_method (backend));
+
   clutter_text_set_buffer (self, NULL);
   clutter_text_set_input_interceptor (self, NULL);
 
